CAT = "abgIndustry"; SEG = "IND"
Q = [
("Under the Security Services and Investigators Act, you need a licence to patrol or guard another person's property when:",
 "It is paid work", ["You carry a baton", "You work night shifts", "You wear a uniform"],
 "Section 3 of the Act requires a licence to patrol, guard or provide security for another person's property for remuneration. Paid work is the trigger, not the shift or the kit."),
("A worker who prevents loss at a retail store while dressed in plain clothes needs which licence?",
 "Loss prevention", ["Executive security", "Alarm responder", "Patrol dog handler"],
 "Section 6 covers preventing or detecting loss of commercial, industrial or retail property in plain clothes. That is the loss prevention licence."),
("Which of these is a separate licence class, not one of the security services licence types?",
 "Investigator", ["Executive security", "Patrol dog handler", "Alarm responder"],
 "The Ministerial Regulation lists investigator, security services, locksmith, automotive lock bypass and training licences as classes. Executive security, patrol dog handler and alarm responder are types of security services licence."),
("What is the minimum age to be issued an individual security licence in Alberta?",
 "18", ["16", "19", "21"],
 "An applicant must prove they have reached the age of majority, which is 18 in Alberta. Alberta's licence page also says applicants must be over 18."),
("An individual security licence may be issued for a term of up to:",
 "2 years", ["1 year", "3 years", "5 years"],
 "Section 9 of the Ministerial Regulation allows an individual licence for up to 2 years. Up to 3 years is the term for a business licence."),
("A guard working in Canada on a work permit is issued a licence. The licence:",
 "Ends with the permit", ["Lasts 2 years regardless", "Ends after 6 months", "Ends when the guard asks"],
 "Section 9(3) of the Ministerial Regulation makes the licence expire with the Canada work permit."),
("An individual security licence is valid only while the licensee:",
 "Works for a licensed firm", ["Lives within Alberta", "Works at one site only", "Holds a driver's licence"],
 "Section 11 of the Ministerial Regulation says an individual licence is valid only while the licensee is employed or engaged by a business licensee."),
("Can a licensed guard work for two licensed security companies at the same time?",
 "Yes, it is allowed", ["No, only one at a time", "Only with two licences", "Only after one year"],
 "Section 12(2) of the Ministerial Regulation lets an individual licensee work for more than one business licensee, at the same time or one after the other."),
("A friend who just finished the course asks to borrow your licence for one shift. You should:",
 "Refuse; it can't be shared", ["Lend it for that shift", "Lend it if your boss agrees", "Lend it to a classmate only"],
 "Section 17 says a licence is not transferable, and section 39 makes it an offence to let another person use your licence."),
("You are charged with a Criminal Code offence. The Registrar must get your written report within:",
 "24 hours", ["48 hours", "7 days", "30 days"],
 "Section 3(1) of the Security Services and Investigators Regulation requires a written report of an arrest or charge within 24 hours."),
("You move to a new home address. How long do you have to report it to the Registrar in writing?",
 "30 days", ["24 hours", "7 days", "Until renewal"],
 "Section 18 of the Act and section 3(3) of the Regulation require a written report of a change in information within 30 days of the change."),
("You lose your licence card. How must you tell the Registrar?",
 "In writing, in 24 hours", ["By phone, in 24 hours", "In writing, in 30 days", "In person at renewal time"],
 "The Regulation and the Ministerial Regulation both require the loss to be reported to the Registrar, in writing, within 24 hours."),
("The Registrar may refuse a licence application from a person who:",
 "Faces a criminal charge", ["Has no driver's licence", "Once worked in BC", "Rents their home"],
 "Section 16(1)(f) lets the Registrar refuse an applicant who has been charged with a criminal offence. Not driving or renting is no ground."),
("The Registrar may suspend or cancel a guard's licence when the guard:",
 "Breaks the conduct code", ["Changes to a new employer", "Takes a second job", "Works only night shifts"],
 "Section 20(d) of the Act lets the Registrar suspend or cancel a licence for failing to comply with the code of conduct. Changing or adding employers is allowed."),
("Your licence is suspended. Under the Act you must:",
 "Return it right away", ["Keep it until a review", "Give it to your employer", "Return it at renewal"],
 "Section 21 requires a licensee whose licence is suspended or cancelled to return it to the Registrar forthwith."),
("The Registrar refuses to renew your licence. You may ask for a review, in writing, from:",
 "The Director", ["Your employer", "The police", "A provincial judge"],
 "Section 23 lets an applicant ask the Director to review the Registrar's decision within 30 days. The Director's decision is final."),
("Which title is a licensed Alberta guard NOT allowed to use?",
 "Security officer", ["Security guard", "Security agent", "Loss prevention worker"],
 "Section 40 bars the terms private detective, law enforcement officer, protection officer and security officer. Security guard and security agent appear on approved uniforms."),
("Under section 37 of the Act, a licensee must never:",
 "Claim to do police work", ["Refuse entry to a site", "Ask to see an event ticket", "Keep a duty notebook"],
 "Section 37 says a licensee shall not hold out that they provide services or duties ordinarily performed by police."),
("A store manager asks you, the guard, to collect an overdue account from a customer. You:",
 "May not act as a collector", ["May, if the store pays you", "May, while in uniform", "May, with a written note"],
 "Section 36 bars a licensee from acting as a collection agency or collector of debts, paid or not."),
("On a security services worker's shirt or jacket, the word SECURITY must appear on:",
 "Front, back and shoulders", ["The front and back only", "Both shoulders only", "The back and one sleeve"],
 "Section 21(3)(d) of the Ministerial Regulation requires SECURITY, SECURITY GUARD or SECURITY AGENT on the front, back and both shoulders."),
("The lettering on the back of a security services uniform must be at least:",
 "5 cm high", ["1.5 cm high", "10 cm high", "2.5 cm high"],
 "Back lettering must be upper case and not less than 5 centimetres high. Lettering on the front and shoulders must be at least 1.5 centimetres."),
("The shoulder flash on a security services worker's uniform must clearly show:",
 "The employer's name", ["The guard's licence number", "The client's company logo", "The Alberta coat of arms"],
 "Section 21(3)(e) requires a shoulder flash on the upper sleeve that displays the business licensee's name and does not resemble a police flash."),
("A security company designs a new uniform. The Ministerial Regulation says it must not:",
 "Look like police dress", ["Be any colour but grey", "Show the company name", "Show any rank markings"],
 "A uniform may be any colour and may show rank markings, but section 21(2) bars a uniform that resembles one used by police or other law enforcement."),
("Which licence type is exempt from the uniform rules?",
 "Loss prevention worker", ["Alarm responder", "Patrol dog handler", "General security services"],
 "Section 22 exempts executive security workers, loss prevention workers, investigators, locksmiths and lock bypass workers from the uniform rules."),
("An employer requires its executive security workers to wear a uniform. That uniform:",
 "Must meet the rules", ["May look like police dress", "Needs no lettering at all", "Is up to the client alone"],
 "Section 22(2) says that if an executive security or loss prevention worker is required to wear a uniform, it must comply with section 21."),
("A badge may be used in security work only when it is:",
 "Shown with your licence", ["Pinned to your uniform", "Bought from a supplier", "Shown instead of your card"],
 "Section 23 says a badge must be issued by the employer, may not be attached to the uniform, and must only be shown together with the licence identification card."),
("While on duty, what must you do with your licence identification card?",
 "Carry it; show on request", ["Leave it at the office", "Show it to police only", "Carry a photocopy instead"],
 "Section 31(3) of the Act and section 24(2) of the Ministerial Regulation require the licensee to carry the card and produce it to any person on request."),
("A security services worker may be authorized to carry a baton no longer than:",
 "26 inches", ["20 inches", "30 inches", "36 inches"],
 "Section 9(1)(a) of the Security Services and Investigators Regulation allows batons not longer than 26 inches when the licence authorizes it."),
("A guard authorized to carry a baton must complete an approved recertification course every:",
 "36 months", ["12 months", "24 months", "60 months"],
 "Section 14(4) of the Ministerial Regulation requires baton recertification every 36 months."),
("A guard may carry a restricted weapon or prohibited device only with authorization from:",
 "The chief firearms officer", ["The site's main client", "Their shift supervisor", "A senior company officer"],
 "Section 10 of the Security Services and Investigators Regulation bars restricted weapons and prohibited devices unless the chief firearms officer under the Firearms Act authorizes them."),
("You see a co-worker fill in patrol times that never happened. The code of conduct bars you from:",
 "Keeping it quiet", ["Reporting it in writing", "Telling your supervisor", "Noting it in your book"],
 "The code of conduct required by section 20 prohibits withholding or suppressing information, complaints or reports about another licensee."),
("A written complaint about an individual guard is first made to:",
 "The guard's employer", ["The Registrar's office", "The local police", "The site's client"],
 "Section 24 of the Act says a complaint about an individual licensee goes in writing to the licensee's employer. Complaints about a business licensee go to the Registrar."),
("A member of the public has how long to make a complaint about a guard's conduct?",
 "90 days", ["30 days", "1 year", "14 days"],
 "Section 24 allows a written complaint within 90 days after the action or circumstance that gave rise to it."),
("After receiving a complaint about one of its guards, the employer must acknowledge it in writing within:",
 "30 days", ["10 days", "90 days", "60 days"],
 "Section 26 of the Ministerial Regulation requires written acknowledgement within 30 days. The employer then has 90 days to dispose of the complaint."),
("Which person is NOT allowed to hold a security licence?",
 "A city police constable", ["A peace officer", "A retired army officer", "A college student"],
 "Section 29 of the Ministerial Regulation bars police officers, sheriffs, bailiffs and debt collectors. A peace officer may hold an individual licence."),
("While on duty, a general training licensee may not:",
 "Carry handcuffs or a baton", ["Wear the employer's uniform", "Patrol with a mentor", "Make notebook entries"],
 "Section 16(4) of the Ministerial Regulation says a general training licensee may not carry handcuffs or a baton and may not drive a vehicle."),
]
